From c87e6764ef702cd7433586df2509ee25a704768d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vitoegg <vitoegg@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix cache: dump the stored time of each entry

readDump restores msg_stored_time, but writeDump never wrote it, so
every entry loaded from a dump was stored at the Unix epoch. Subtracting
the time since then from its TTLs left them all at 1 second until the
entry was refreshed, which made clients query again for every restored
entry after a restart.

Write the stored time with each entry. Entries loaded from a dump of an
older build still lack it, until they are refreshed from upstream.

Signed-off-by: vitoegg <vitoegg@gmail.com>
---
 plugin/executable/cache/cache.go | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/plugin/executable/cache/cache.go b/plugin/executable/cache/cache.go
index 63272ed..1d401e1 100644
--- a/plugin/executable/cache/cache.go
+++ b/plugin/executable/cache/cache.go
@@ -502,6 +502,7 @@ func (c *Cache) writeDump(w io.Writer) (int, error) {
 			Key:                 []byte(k),
 			CacheExpirationTime: cacheExpirationTime.Unix(),
 			MsgExpirationTime:   v.expirationTime.Unix(),
+			MsgStoredTime:       v.storedTime.Unix(),
 			Msg:                 msg,
 		}
 		block.Entries = append(block.Entries, e)
